# Scene
trueqbit with Claude (Opus 5.5), 2026-11-18, on #1627: the code review
(/code-review medium) of #1627's two commits found task.h and when_all.h
in functional/ but gated by SQLITE_ORM_WITH_ASYNC alone.

# Decided
- trueqbit: double guard rather than SQLITE_ORM_CPP20_COROUTINES_SUPPORTED
  alone: the types are general-purpose C++, but make sense only in the
  purview of sqlite_orm's asynchronous storage; the second guard carries
  a comment saying so.
- trueqbit: review findings on #1627's earlier commits are corrected in
  succeeding commits this time, without rewriting them (fnc12 is
  requested as reviewer).

# Discussed
- SQLITE_ORM_WITH_ASYNC already implies coroutine support
  (config/capabilities.h), so the outer guard states the requirement
  rather than narrowing anything. pre-commit.sh exits 0.
